* Exercise: Web Crawler

In this exercise you'll use Go's concurrency features to parallelize a web crawler.

Modify the ⟪GTI18N_bb686393_000001⟫Crawl⟪GTI18N_bb686393_000002⟫ function to fetch URLs in parallel without fetching the same URL twice.

⟪GTI18N_bb686393_000003⟫Hint⟪GTI18N_bb686393_000004⟫: you can keep a cache of the URLs that have been fetched on a map, but maps alone are not
safe for concurrent use!

